2026-11-06T03:00:24.6120855Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6129567Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6130476Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6131422Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6132151Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6132443Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6132841Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6133166Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6133846Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6134190Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6134382Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6134856Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6135141Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6135458Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6135894Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:00:24.6136056Z 
